hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1492","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Abu Ashana, that he heard Uqba bin Amir Al-Juhani narrates, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “If a man purifies himself, then passes to the mosque and leads the prayer, it is written for him His writer, or his writers, assign ten good deeds for every step they take towards the mosque, and the one who sits pays attention to prayer like an obedient woman, and he is recorded as one of the worshippers. From where he leaves his house until he returns.”"
